There has to be recognition by law that the careless infliction of the kind of damages in suit on the class of per- son to which the claimant be longs by the class of person to which the de- fendant belongs is actionable;
(2) breach of duty of care by the defendant, i.e. that it failed to meas- ure up to the standard set by law;
(3) a casual connection between the defendant's careless conduct and the damage;
(4) that the particular kind of damage to the particular claimant is not so unforeseeable as to be too remote."
